CBSE MCQ STRUCTURAL CHECKS (apply before scoring)
- Exactly 4 options labelled A, B, C, D. Fewer/more = bad.
- answer must be exactly one of A/B/C/D and the answer string must appear as a key in options.
- options must not include any phrasing in curriculum_constraints.forbidden_patterns. Presence = bad.
- option lengths must be within ~30% of each other. Wild length variance = upgrade (grammar/structure issue).
- Numerical answers must include SI units when the chapter uses units. Naked numbers when units are required = upgrade.

CBSE CONTENT CHECKS
- The stem and explanation must use IUPAC nomenclature when the chapter does (prefer IUPAC over trivial/common names). Mismatch = upgrade (terminology).
- Chemical species in answer should be written as formulas, not common names, when the chapter does so. Mismatch = upgrade.
- The question must be answerable from CHAPTER KNOWLEDGE alone. Reliance on facts outside the chapter (even if true) = hallucination = bad.
- For Class 12 specifically: pure-recall items in difficulty levels above "easy" = upgrade (move-to-easy reason).

CBSE DISTRACTOR QUALITY
- Each distractor should map to a documented Class 12 misconception (e.g. molarity vs molality, sign error in delta T, wrong formula constant). Throwaway distractors not mapped to a misconception = upgrade with reason "weak_distractor".
- "All of the above" / "None of the above" / "Both A and C" style options = bad (CBSE sample papers don't use these).

DUPLICATE JUDGMENT (uses the deterministic candidates already retrieved)
- duplicate_status = "duplicate" only when one of candidate_duplicates is semantically identical (same concept tested with the same expected answer reasoning). duplicate_score must reflect your conviction.
- duplicate_status = "near_duplicate" for same-concept-different-numbers items at the same difficulty. duplicate_status = "unique" otherwise.
- duplicate_candidate_ids[] must be a subset of the candidate question_ids you were given. Never invent IDs.

TAGGING RULES (apply deterministically; ties default to "upgrade")
- good: factual_correctness_score >= 0.85 AND answer_correctness_score >= 0.9 AND board_alignment_score >= 0.8 AND class_alignment_score >= 0.8 AND difficulty_alignment_score >= 0.8 AND grammar_score >= 0.85 AND ambiguity_score <= 0.2 AND hallucination_flag = false AND duplicate_status = "unique" AND final_include = true AND ALL structural checks pass.
- bad: hallucination_flag = true OR duplicate_status = "duplicate" OR answer_correctness_score < 0.6 OR factual_correctness_score < 0.6 OR any structural check fails (wrong option count, answer not in options, forbidden option phrase, fewer than 4 options) OR outside-chapter.
- upgrade: everything else (minor issues, salvageable with rewriting).

STRICT OUTPUT RULES
- Return ONE results[] entry for EVERY draft_question_id provided. Missing entries cause the workflow to post-tag them as "upgrade".
- duplicate_candidate_ids[] must be a subset of provided candidate ids. Do not invent ids.
- Output JSON ONLY, matching the schema above. No markdown. No prose. No code fences.
